{
  "help": {
    "exit": 0,
    "exception": null,
    "stdout": "usage: export_idml.py [-h] [--model MODEL] [--region REGION] [--lang LANG]\n                      [--category CATEGORY] [--data-root DATA_ROOT]\n                      [--out OUT] [--bundle-root BUNDLE_ROOT]\n                      [--mode {production,flow,both}] [--check CHECK]\n                      [--template TEMPLATE] [--assembly-plan ASSEMBLY_PLAN]\n                      [--layout-params-csv LAYOUT_PARAMS_CSV]\n                      [--layout-params-overlay LAYOUT_PARAMS_OVERLAY]\n\nIDML exporter — route B of the InDesign handoff plan. Produces an editable\n.idml package from the same prepared-bundle IR as LaTeX, so designers can\nfine-tune pipeline output instead of retouching PDFs. Usage: python\ntools/export_idml.py --model JE-1000F --region US [--lang en] [--data-root\ndata/phase2] [--out docs/_build/.../manual.idml] python tools/export_idml.py\n--check <file.idml> # structural validation\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --model MODEL         product model registered in the build target\n  --region REGION\n  --lang LANG\n  --category CATEGORY   product line, from build.skeleton_family; carriers\n                        branch on it as '.. only:: category_<value>'. Left\n                        unset a carrier's category branch is simply absent, so\n                        build.py always passes the configured value.\n  --data-root DATA_ROOT\n  --out OUT\n  --bundle-root BUNDLE_ROOT\n                        Prepared rst bundle dir (default:\n                        docs/_build/<model>/<region>/<lang>/rst); prose pages\n                        are skipped if absent\n  --mode {production,flow,both}, --idml-mode {production,flow,both}\n                        IDML export mode; production preserves historical\n                        behavior.\n  --check CHECK         validate an existing .idml and exit\n  --template TEMPLATE   bake production idml into this template .idml (pre-\n                        styled)\n  --assembly-plan ASSEMBLY_PLAN\n                        configured candidate target assembly JSON; approved\n                        reference contracts still take precedence\n  --layout-params-csv LAYOUT_PARAMS_CSV\n                        baseline layout-token CSV selected by the build config\n  --layout-params-overlay LAYOUT_PARAMS_OVERLAY\n                        additive IDML composition-token CSV; may be repeated\n",
    "stderr": "",
    "events": []
  },
